================================================================================
HOW DOES CSS KNOW IT IS PURCHASED?
================================================================================

It comes from React:

className={
  `item-card ${
    item.purchased
      ? 'purchased'
      : ''
  }`
}


If:

item.purchased === false


HTML class effectively becomes:

item-card


If:

item.purchased === true


it becomes:

item-card purchased


Then this selector matches:

.item-card.purchased
.item-name


================================================================================
STRIKETHROUGH FORMULA
================================================================================

item.purchased
      ↓
true
      ↓
"purchased" class
      ↓
.item-card.purchased .item-name
      ↓
text-decoration: line-through


