PART 6: CHANGING CHECKBOX COLOR
================================================================================

Native checkboxes can use:

accent-color


Example:

.item-checkbox {

  accent-color:
    #4caf50;
}


This customizes the checkbox's accent.

For our purchased state, green provides clear visual reinforcement.


================================================================================
IMPORTANT CORRECTION
================================================================================

The original lesson described:

Unchecked:
Blue


Checked:
Green


using:

.item-checkbox {

  accent-color:
    #667eea;
}


.item-checkbox:checked {

  accent-color:
    #4caf50;
}


But `accent-color` primarily affects the native control's accent presentation.

It does NOT mean browsers will always draw an unchecked checkbox as a blue
circle.


The exact native checkbox appearance depends on the browser/platform.


A safer description is:

UNCHECKED:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Native/browser checkbox appearance


CHECKED:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Green accent where supported by the native control


================================================================================
CHECKBOX CSS
================================================================================

.item-checkbox {

  width:
    20px;

  height:
    20px;

  cursor:
    pointer;

  accent-color:
    #4caf50;
}


.item-checkbox:hover {

  transform:
    scale(1.08);
}


.item-checkbox:focus-visible {

  outline:
    3px solid #667eea;

  outline-offset:
    3px;
}


================================================================================
DO WE NEED :checked accent-color?
================================================================================

Not necessarily.

This is enough:

.item-checkbox {

  accent-color:
    #4caf50;
}


The browser applies the accent to the native checked state.


If you intentionally want state-specific CSS:

.item-checkbox:checked {

  accent-color:
    #4caf50;
}


is valid.


But don't assume the unchecked native appearance can be completely redesigned
through accent-color alone.


================================================================================
CHECKBOX STATE
================================================================================

React controls:

checked={
  item.purchased
}


CSS controls:

accent-color


So:

item.purchased
      ↓
checked
      ↓
Native Checked State
      ↓
Accent Presentation


================================================================================
CHECKBOX ACCESSIBILITY
================================================================================

Do not remove the native checkbox just to make styling easier unless you are
prepared to recreate all required interaction and accessibility behavior.


The native checkbox already provides:

• Checkbox semantics

• Checked/unchecked state

• Keyboard operation

• Focus support


For this app:

NATIVE CHECKBOX
+
accent-color
+
visible focus


is a simple and robust approach.


