================================================================================
WHY REDUCE THE OPACITY LESS AGGRESSIVELY?
================================================================================

The original CSS used:

opacity:
0.6


on the entire purchased card.


This also fades:

• Text

• Checkbox

• Delete button

• Focus/interaction visuals


A very low parent opacity can make readable/actionable content unnecessarily
weak.


This cleaned version uses:

opacity:
0.78


plus targeted:

• Color changes

• Background changes

• Strikethrough

• Border changes


This keeps the purchased state visually different while retaining useful
contrast and interaction visibility.


================================================================================
WHY REMOVE fadeOut ANIMATION?
================================================================================

The original lesson used:

@keyframes fadeOut


on every purchased item.


But no explicit animation is required for a strikethrough state.

The existing transitions already provide gentle feedback.


Simpler:

State Changes
     ↓
CSS Properties Transition


instead of:

State Changes
     ↓
Extra Keyframe Animation
     ↓
Opacity Animation


This also reduces unnecessary motion.


